 },
 "capsule": "This Venezuela denotes the state that emerged from Gran Colombia's 1830 dissolution under José Antonio Páez, consolidating through the nineteenth-century caudillo era, the long Juan Vicente Gómez dictatorship (1908–1935), and the 1958 transition to elected civilian rule. From 1999 it was reconstituted as the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela under Hugo Chávez and, after his 2013 death, Nicolás Maduro, a period marked by economic collapse and mass emigration in the 2010s–2020s. It is distinct from the short-lived revolutionary First and Second Republics of 1811–1814 that share this Wikidata identifier.",
 "citations": [
